#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using Qiskit to implement ideas from the entanglement in action lesson."
msgstr "量子もつれの応用レッスンのアイデアをQiskitで実装します。"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation"
msgstr "Qiskit実装"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore ebit operatorname */}\n"
"In this lesson, we implement some of the ideas from the lesson on entanglement in action, using Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore ebit operatorname */}\n"
"このレッスンでは、量子もつれの応用レッスンで紹介したアイデアの一部をQiskitを使って実装します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is a quantum circuit implementation of the teleportation protocol.\n"
msgstr "テレポーテーションプロトコルの量子Circuit実装を以下に示します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/3eb41206-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/3eb41206-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit makes use of a few features of Qiskit that we've not yet seen in previous lessons, including the `barrier` and `if_test` functions.\n"
"The `barrier` function creates a visual separation making the circuit diagram more readable, and it also prevents Qiskit from performing various simplifications and optimizations across the barrier during compilation when circuits are run on real hardware.\n"
"The `if_test` function applies an operation conditionally depending on a classical bit or register.\n"
msgstr ""
"このCircuitでは、前のレッスンで扱っていないQiskitのいくつかの機能を使用しています。具体的には `barrier` 関数と `if_test` 関数です。\n"
"`barrier` 関数は視覚的な区切りを作ってCircuit図を読みやすくするとともに、実際のハードウェア上でCircuitを実行する際のコンパイル時に、Qiskitがバリアをまたいだ各種の簡略化・最適化を行うのを防ぎます。\n"
"`if_test` 関数は、古典ビットまたはレジスタの値に応じて条件付きで操作を適用します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit first initializes $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ to be in a $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state (which is not part of the protocol itself), followed by Alice's operations, then her measurements, and finally Bob's operations.\n"
"To test that the protocol works correctly, we'll apply a randomly generated single-qubit gate to the initialized $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state of $\\mathsf{Q}$ to obtain a random quantum state vector to be teleported. By applying the inverse (as in, the conjugate transpose) of that gate to $\\mathsf{B}$ after the protocol is run, we can verify that the state was teleported by measuring to see that it has returned to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state.\n"
msgstr ""
"このCircuitはまず $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ を $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ 状態に初期化し（これ自体はプロトコルの一部ではありません）、次にアリスの操作、その後測定、最後にボブの操作を行います。\n"
"プロトコルが正しく動作することを確認するために、$\\mathsf{Q}$ の初期化された $\\vert 0\\rangle$ 状態にランダムに生成した1Qubit Gateを適用し、テレポートする乱数状態ベクトルを得ます。プロトコル実行後にそのGateの逆演算（すなわち共役転置）を $\\mathsf{B}$ に適用することで、状態が $\\vert 0\\rangle$ に戻ったかどうかを測定してテレポーテーションを検証できます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First we'll randomly choose a unitary qubit gate.\n"
msgstr "まず、ランダムなユニタリ1Qubit Gateを選択します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0.9897212158 & -0.0195080103 - 0.141673401 i  \\\\\n"
" 0.0603319186 + 0.1296609988 i & -0.8319925233 + 0.5360378028 i  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0.9897212158 & -0.0195080103 - 0.141673401 i  \\\\\n"
" 0.0603319186 + 0.1296609988 i & -0.8319925233 + 0.5360378028 i  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll create a new testing circuit that first applies our random gate to $\\mathsf{Q},$ then runs the teleportation circuit, and finally applies the inverse of our random gate to the qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ and measures.\n"
"The outcome should be $0$ with certainty.\n"
msgstr ""
"次に、新しいテスト用Circuitを作成します。このCircuitはまず $\\mathsf{Q}$ にランダムなGateを適用し、テレポーテーションCircuitを実行し、最後にランダムなGateの逆演算をQubit $\\mathsf{B}$ に適用して測定します。\n"
"結果は確実に $0$ になるはずです。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/ce7568a0-23d2-41d2-aadc-ad898b3a7ebe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/ce7568a0-23d2-41d2-aadc-ad898b3a7ebe-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, let's run the Aer simulator on this circuit and plot a histogram of the outputs.\n"
"We'll see the statistics for all three classical bits:\n"
"the bottom/leftmost bit should always be $0,$ indicating that the qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ was successfully teleported into $\\mathsf{B},$ while the other two bits should be roughly uniform.\n"
msgstr ""
"では、このCircuitに対してAerシミュレーターを実行し、出力のヒストグラムをプロットしてみましょう。\n"
"3つの古典ビットすべての統計が表示されます。一番下（左端）のビットは常に $0$ となり、Qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ が $\\mathsf{B}$ に正常にテレポートされたことを示します。一方、残りの2つのビットはほぼ一様に分布するはずです。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/4db32a9d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/4db32a9d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also filter the statistics to focus solely on the test result qubit "
"if we wish, like this:\n"
msgstr "必要に応じて、テスト結果のQubitのみに絞って統計をフィルタリングすることもできます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/b3e3be9a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/b3e3be9a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"
msgstr "超高密度符号化 {#superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Superdense coding is a protocol that, in some sense, achieves a complementary aim to teleportation.\n"
"Rather than allowing for the transmission of one qubit using two classical bits of communication (at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement), it allows for the transmission of two classical bits using one qubit of quantum communication (again, at the cost of one e-bit of entanglement).\n"
msgstr ""
"超高密度符号化（Superdense coding）は、ある意味でテレポーテーションと相補的な目的を達成するプロトコルです。\n"
"テレポーテーションが2古典ビットの通信を用いて1Qubitを送信できる（1 e-bitのもつれコストあり）のに対し、超高密度符号化では1Qubitの量子通信を用いて2古典ビットを送信できます（こちらも1 e-bitのもつれコストあり）。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, we have a sender (Alice) and a receiver (Bob) that share one e-bit of entanglement.\n"
"According to the conventions in place for the lesson, this means that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Alice wishes to transmit two classical bits to Bob, which we'll denote by $c$ and $d,$ and she will accomplish this by sending him one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"より詳しく説明すると、送信者（アリス）と受信者（ボブ）が1 e-bitのもつれを共有しています。\n"
"レッスン内の規約に従い、アリスはQubit $\\mathsf{A}$ を、ボブはQubit $\\mathsf{B}$ を持ち、ペア $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ は状態 $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ にあります。\n"
"アリスは $c$ と $d$ で表される2つの古典ビットをボブに送りたいと考えており、1つのQubitを送ることでこれを実現します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is reasonable to view this feat as being less interesting than the one that teleportation accomplishes.\n"
"Sending qubits is likely to be so much more difficult than sending classical bits for the foreseeable future that trading one qubit of quantum communication for two bits of classical communication, at the cost of an e-bit no less, hardly seems worth it.\n"
"However, this does not imply that superdense coding is not interesting, for it most certainly is.\n"
msgstr ""
"この成果は、テレポーテーションが達成するものほど興味深くないと見なすこともできます。\n"
"当面の間、Qubitを送ることは古典ビットを送ることよりはるかに困難になると思われるため、e-bitのコストを払ってまで1Qubitの量子通信を2ビットの古典通信と交換することは、ほとんど割に合わないように思えます。\n"
"しかし、だからといって超高密度符号化が興味深くないということにはなりません。これは非常に興味深いプロトコルです。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fitting the theme of the lesson, one reason why superdense coding is interesting is that it demonstrates a concrete and (in the context of information theory) rather striking use of entanglement.\n"
"A famous theorem in quantum information theory, known as *Holevo's theorem*, implies that without the use of a shared entangled state, it is impossible to communicate more than one bit of classical information by sending a single qubit.\n"
"(Holevo's theorem is more general than this.\n"
"Its precise statement is technical and requires explanation, but this is one consequence of it.)\n"
"So, through superdense coding, shared entanglement effectively allows for the *doubling* of the classical information-carrying capacity of sending qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"レッスンのテーマに即して言えば、超高密度符号化が興味深い理由の一つは、もつれの具体的かつ（情報理論の文脈では）かなり印象的な利用例を示しているからです。\n"
"*Holevoの定理*として知られる量子情報理論の有名な定理によると、共有されたもつれ状態を使わない場合、1Qubitを送ることで送信できる古典情報量は1ビットを超えることができません。\n"
"（Holevoの定理はこれよりも一般的です。正確な表現は技術的であり説明が必要ですが、これはその一つの帰結です。）\n"
"つまり、超高密度符号化により、共有もつれはQubitを送ることで伝達できる古典情報容量を実質的に*2倍*にすることができます。\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Protocol {#protocol}"
msgstr "プロトコル {#protocol}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following quantum circuit diagram describes the superdense coding "
"protocol:\n"
msgstr "次の量子Circuit図は超高密度符号化プロトコルを描写しています。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/superdense-"
"coding.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Superdense coding circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/superdense-"
"coding.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In words, here is what Alice does:\n"
msgstr "アリスの操作を言葉で説明すると以下の通りです。\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $d=1,$ Alice performs a $Z$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if $d=0$"
" she does not).\n"
msgstr ""
"$d=1$ の場合、アリスは自分のQubit $\\mathsf{A}$ に $Z$ Gateを適用します（$d=0$ の場合は何もしません）。\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $c=1,$ Alice performs an $X$ gate on her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ (and if "
"$c=0$ she does not).\n"
msgstr ""
"$c=1$ の場合、アリスは自分のQubit $\\mathsf{A}$ に $X$ Gateを適用します（$c=0$ の場合は何もしません）。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice then sends her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob.\n"
msgstr "アリスはその後、自分のQubit $\\mathsf{A}$ をボブに送ります。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bob does when he receives the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ is to first perform a controlled-NOT gate, with $\\mathsf{A}$ being the control and $\\mathsf{B}$ being the target, and then he applies a Hadamard gate to $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"He then measures $\\mathsf{B}$ to obtain $c$ and $\\mathsf{A}$ to obtain $d,$ with standard basis measurements in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"ボブはQubit $\\mathsf{A}$ を受け取ると、まず $\\mathsf{A}$ を制御、$\\mathsf{B}$ をターゲットとする制御NOTゲートを適用し、続いて $\\mathsf{A}$ にアダマールゲートを適用します。\n"
"その後、$\\mathsf{B}$ を測定して $c$ を、$\\mathsf{A}$ を測定して $d$ を得ます。いずれも標準基底測定です。\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "解析 {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The idea behind this protocol is simple:\n"
"Alice effectively chooses which Bell state she would like to be sharing with Bob,\n"
"she sends Bob her qubit, and Bob measures to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
msgstr ""
"このプロトコルの考え方はシンプルです。\n"
"アリスはボブと共有したいベル状態を実質的に選択し、\n"
"自分のQubitをボブに送ります。ボブはどのベル状態をアリスが選んだかを測定で判定します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, they initially share $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ and depending upon the bits $c$ and $d,$ Alice either leaves this state alone or shifts it to one of the other Bell states by applying $\\mathbb{I},$ $X,$ $Z,$ or $XZ$ to her qubit\n"
"$\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"つまり、はじめに $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ を共有している状態から、ビット $c$ と $d$ "
"の値に応じて、アリスは自分のQubit $\\mathsf{A}$ に $\\mathbb{I}$、$X$、$Z$、または $XZ$ "
"を適用することで、この状態をそのままにするか他のベル状態に変換します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes XZ) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^-\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's actions have the following effects on the four Bell states:\n"
msgstr "ボブの操作は4つのベル状態に対して次の効果をもたらします。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle & \\mapsto \\vert 10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle & \\mapsto -\\vert 11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be checked directly, by computing the results of Bob's operations "
"on these states one at a time.\n"
msgstr "これは各状態に対してボブの操作の結果を直接計算することで確認できます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, when Bob performs his measurements, he is able to determine which Bell state Alice chose.\n"
"To verify that the protocol works correctly is a matter of checking each case:\n"
msgstr ""
"したがって、ボブが測定を行うと、アリスがどのベル状態を選んだかを判定できます。\n"
"プロトコルが正しく動作することを確認するには、各ケースを個別に検証します。\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 00,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $\\vert 00\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 00.$\n"
msgstr ""
"$cd = 00$ の場合、ボブが $\\mathsf{A}$ を受け取った時点での $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ の状態は "
"$\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ です。ボブはこの状態を $\\vert 00\\rangle$ に変換し、$cd = 00$ "
"を得ます。\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 01,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $\\vert 01\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 01.$\n"
msgstr ""
"$cd = 01$ の場合、ボブが $\\mathsf{A}$ を受け取った時点での $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ の状態は "
"$\\vert \\phi^-\\rangle$ です。ボブはこの状態を $\\vert 01\\rangle$ に変換し、$cd = 01$ "
"を得ます。\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 10,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $\\vert 10\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 10.$\n"
msgstr ""
"$cd = 10$ の場合、ボブが $\\mathsf{A}$ を受け取った時点での $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ の状態は "
"$\\vert \\psi^+\\rangle$ です。ボブはこの状態を $\\vert 10\\rangle$ に変換し、$cd = 10$ "
"を得ます。\n"

#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $cd = 11,$ then the state of $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ when Bob "
"receives $\\mathsf{A}$ is $\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.$ He transforms this state"
" into $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ and obtains $cd = 11.$ (The negative-one phase "
"factor has no effect here.)\n"
msgstr ""
"$cd = 11$ の場合、ボブが $\\mathsf{A}$ を受け取った時点での $(\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{A})$ の状態は "
"$\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$ です。ボブはこの状態を $-\\vert 11\\rangle$ に変換し、$cd = 11$ "
"を得ます。（マイナス1の位相因子はここでは影響しません。）\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding implementation {#superdense-coding-implementation}"
msgstr "超高密度符号化の実装 {#superdense-coding-implementation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is a simple implementation of superdense coding where we specify the "
"circuit itself depending on the bits to be transmitted. First we'll choose "
"two bits to be transmitted. (Later we'll choose them randomly, but for now "
"we'll just make an arbitrary choice.)\n"
msgstr ""
"以下は超高密度符号化の簡単な実装です。送信するビットに応じてCircuitを構成します。まず送信する2ビットを選択します（後ほどランダムに選びますが、ここではとりあえず任意の値を設定します）。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll build the circuit accordingly. Here we'll allow Qiskit to use the "
"default names for the qubits: $\\mathsf{q}_0$ for the top qubit and "
"$\\mathsf{q}_1$ for the bottom one.\n"
msgstr ""
"次に、それに応じてCircuitを構築します。ここではQiskitのデフォルト名をQubitに使用します。上のQubitが "
"$\\mathsf{q}_0$、下のQubitが $\\mathsf{q}_1$ となります。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/05ae9b94-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/05ae9b94-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not much is new here, except the `measure_all` function, which measures all "
"of the qubits and puts the results into a single classical register (and "
"therefore having two bits in this case).\n"
msgstr ""
"新しい点としては `measure_all` "
"関数があります。これはすべてのQubitを測定し、結果を1つの古典レジスタに格納します（この場合は2ビットになります）。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Running the Aer simulator produces the expected output.\n"
msgstr "Aerシミュレーターを実行すると、期待通りの出力が得られます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/6309a901-c3da-4b7d-b762-c6a7b542457b-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/6309a901-c3da-4b7d-b762-c6a7b542457b-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's use an additional qubit as a random bit generator — essentially to"
" flip fair coins. We'll use it to randomly choose $c$ and $d,$ and then run "
"the superdense coding protocol.\n"
msgstr ""
"次に、追加のQubitをランダムビット生成器として使用しましょう。これはコインを公平に投げることに相当します。これを使って $c$ と $d$ "
"をランダムに選択し、超高密度符号化プロトコルを実行します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/06e461e9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/qiskit-implementation/extracted-"
"outputs/06e461e9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Running the Aer simulator shows the results: Alice and Bob's classical bits "
"always agree.\n"
msgstr "Aerシミュレーターを実行すると、アリスとボブの古典ビットが常に一致していることが確認できます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
